  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1970-p22.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(S_m=\\frac{m(m+1)}{2}.\\) Then \\[ \\begin{aligned} 2(S_{3n}-S_n) &=3n(3n+1)\\\\ &\\quad{}-n(n+1)\\\\ &=8n^2+2n. \\end{aligned} \\] Since \\(S_{3n}-S_n=150,\\) this gives \\(4n^2+n=150.\\) Hence \\((n-6)(4n+25)=0,\\) and the positive solution is \\(n=6.\\) Therefore \\[ S_{4n}=S_{24}=\\frac{24\\cdot25}{2}=300. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(1+2+\\cdots+m=\\frac{m(m+1)}{2}\\)",
        "The given difference simplifies to \\(4n^2+n\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
